    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18103" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Fīculnĕus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		ficula, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of the fig-tree</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ligna,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 3, 16, 37</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">folia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					6, 3, 7</span></i>
			.—As <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fīculnĕa</span></b> ,
				ae, f., <i>a
			fig-tree</i>, <i><span class="en">Vulg. Osee, 9, 10</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">id.
				Luc. 13, 7</span></i>.— In the form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ficulnus</span></b> , a, um: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">truncus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					S. 1, 8, 1</span></i>
			.</div>
